B = [
('Thonet', 'Europe', '1850s-1930s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Thonet, bentwood furniture made from steam-bent solid beech rods formed into continuous flowing curves. Slender round-section frames, looping circles and S-scrolls in the backrest, a round or oval seat of woven cane or pressed plywood with tiny perforations, splayed delicate legs joined by a ring brace. Finish is stained dark mahogany brown, walnut or ebonised black with a satin lacquer, with visible screw heads and metal collars at joints. Cafe chairs, rocking chairs and hat stands, light, airy and sculptural, mass-produced Viennese coffeehouse mood, later chrome tubular steel cantilever chairs with cane panels and black leather in the 1920s.'),
('Herman Miller', 'North America', '1950s-60s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Herman Miller, American mid-century modern furniture with molded plywood and fibreglass shells in organic curves, perched on thin wire struts or splayed wooden dowel legs with metal cross braces. Colours are warm walnut, ash and rosewood veneer, black leather with plump cushions, and bright pops of orange, mustard yellow, turquoise and white. Lounge chairs with stacked cushioned panels on a cast aluminium swivel base, bubble-shaped sofas, slatted platform benches, egg-shaped and kidney-shaped forms, exposed joints and brass or chrome hardware. Playful, optimistic, sunlit California living room and office look, clean honest construction, later ergonomic mesh task chairs in graphite with visible skeletal frames.'),
('Knoll', 'North America', '1940s-60s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Knoll, high modernist furniture with polished chrome-plated flat steel bars bent in precise cantilever arcs, supporting thin black or tan leather sling seats and tufted cushions held by visible buttons and straps. Tulip-shaped pedestals with a single white moulded base and a round white marble or laminate tabletop, bent wire diamond-shaped chairs, glass-topped coffee tables on chrome X-frames, sculpted rosewood sideboards. Palette of white, black, chrome, cream and saturated primary upholstery in wool tweed. Minimal, architectural, boardroom and corporate lobby elegance, pared down to structure with sharp crisp edges and mirror shine.'),
('Vitra', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'furniture', 'In the style of Vitra, contemporary design furniture with sculptural moulded polypropylene and plastic shells in matte pastel and primary colours, thin steel rod legs or wooden dowel bases, and playful oversized forms like gnome-shaped stools and spidery floor lamps. Curvy lounge chairs with wrapped upholstery in felt, wool and leather, black ash and oak veneer, white lacquer. Reissued mid-century plywood and fibreglass classics sit beside deconstructed, geometric, exhibition-like pieces. Crisp Swiss and German gallery aesthetic, witty, colourful, clean shadow lines, studio product photography on seamless white backdrops.'),
('Artek', 'Europe', '1930s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Artek, Finnish modernist furniture of pale laminated birch with a distinctive bent L-shaped leg that curls into a smooth scroll beneath the seat. Round three-legged stools, simple tables, cantilevered chairs with lightly curved plywood seats, and hanging pendant lamps. Natural birch, white lacquer, black linoleum tabletops and colourful lacquered legs in red, yellow, blue and green, woven webbing and canvas upholstery in stripes. Warm, humane, Scandinavian functionalism, soft rounded edges, light blond wood grain, nordic apartment and school hall mood.'),
('Fritz Hansen', 'Europe', '1950s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Fritz Hansen, Danish modern furniture with sculptural moulded laminated wood shells in a curvy ant, butterfly or egg silhouette, pinched waist and no visible join between seat and back. Slim chromed steel tube legs on three or four points, upholstery in tight leather or tweed wool, coloured lacquered veneer in black, white, lime green, deep red and warm walnut. Swivel pod chairs on a spiderlike cast aluminium base, generous cushioning, glossy and smooth surfaces. Elegant, airy, hotel lobby and Copenhagen design office feel with smooth organic flow, never fussy.'),
('Carl Hansen', 'Europe', '1950s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Carl Hansen, Danish cabinetmaker furniture in solid oak, teak and walnut with soaked, oiled or soaped finishes showing fine grain. Curved wishbone-shaped backrests with a Y-shaped steam-bent top rail, hand-woven natural paper cord seats, tapered rounded legs, finely crafted pegged joints and visible wood joinery. Low lounge chairs with leather straps, sculptural oak armrests that float, round-edged dining tables. Palette of honey, pale blond, soft brown and cream leather. Calm, tactile, handcrafted, minimalist Scandinavian dining room and living room.'),
('IKEA', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'furniture', 'In the style of IKEA, flat-pack Scandinavian home furnishings in pale birch, pine and white-painted particleboard, with simple rectangular boxes, slim peg or tapered legs and rounded corners. Palette of white, light wood, bright cobalt blue and sunshine yellow, with muted greys, sage and pastel accents in textiles. Modular shelving with open cubbies, lightweight stackable chairs, paper lampshades, striped and checked cotton, simple ceramic mugs in primary colours. Bright, democratic, practical showroom styling, room-set vignettes with cosy rugs, houseplants and minimalist clutter-free surfaces, airy daylight look.'),
('Muji', 'East Asia', '1980s-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Muji, Japanese no-brand minimalism with plain unbleached cotton, linen, recycled paper and natural kraft cardboard. Muted palette of off-white, oatmeal, warm grey, beige, charcoal and navy only, without logos or decoration. Simple rectangular storage boxes in translucent polypropylene, wooden shelves, brown paper tags, clear acrylic organisers, soft washed linen bedding, matte white ceramic and stainless steel utensils. Everything is modest, quiet, functional, evenly lit on clean shelves, restrained packaging with small black sans-serif labelling and a calm shop look.'),
('Cassina', 'Europe', '1960s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Cassina, Italian luxury modernist furniture with deep, plump, tufted leather sofas in cognac, black and cream on thin chrome or lacquered steel frames. Sculptural wooden chairs with ladder backs and pale rush seats, tubular steel stool bases, wide-armed leather armchairs and low lacquered tables with reflective glass tops. Rich materials include walnut, rosewood, polished marble, burnished brass and saddle-stitched hide. Refined, architectural, masculine and expensive, with sharp proportions blending craftsmanship and industrial precision in a Milanese penthouse setting.'),
('Kartell', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'furniture', 'In the style of Kartell, Italian injection-moulded plastic furniture, glossy and translucent polycarbonate in crystal clear, smoky, ruby red, fluorescent orange, lime and acid pink. Chairs with sculptural baroque silhouettes, transparent ghost-like forms, stackable stools, lighting in clear plastic shaped like pleated shades and bulbous gourds. Smooth seamless curves, bright jewel colours, high-gloss reflections and light passing through the material. Playful, fashionable, pop and kitsch with modern luxury, gallery-white showroom photography, reflective floors.'),
('Alessi', 'Europe', '1980s-90s', 'homeware', 'In the style of Alessi, Italian postmodern kitchenware in polished stainless steel with playful anthropomorphic forms, such as kettles with bird-shaped whistles, citrus squeezers with spidery tripod legs, and cheerful little figures that hold corkscrews. Bright resin and plastic accents in red, yellow, pink, blue and green against mirror-polished steel, rounded cones, spheres and cylinders, cute faces and exaggerated spouts. Witty, toy-like and sculptural, domestic objects as pop-art ornaments, cheerful kitchen shelf photography with soft shadows.'),
('Memphis Group', 'Europe', '1980s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Memphis Group, Italian postmodern furniture and objects built from clashing geometric blocks, triangles, cylinders and zigzags. Cheeky laminate in bold squiggle, terrazzo and speckled confetti patterns, in pink, teal, mustard yellow, sky blue, black and white. Wobbly asymmetrical bookshelves shaped like totem figures, cubist sideboards on tapered legs, dayglo plastic lamps, glass vases with stripes and dots. Playful, irreverent, cartoonish 1980s mood, flat saturated colour planes with thick black outlines, kitsch and joyful.'),
('Fornasetti', 'Europe', '1950s', 'homeware', 'In the style of Fornasetti, Italian decorative objects and furniture covered in printed black and white engravings on glossy lacquer, with surreal repeating motifs such as a woman face with half-closed eyes, sun faces, playing cards, butterflies, keys, hands, architectural arches, and classical ruins. Plates, umbrella stands, folding screens, cabinets and trays with gilded edges, deep black, bold red, cream and gold accents. Dense graphic linework, trompe-l oeil, witty and theatrical, cultured Milanese interior, ornamental and mysterious.'),
('Venini', 'Europe', '1930s-50s', 'glass', 'In the style of Venini, Venetian art glass with thin hand-blown walls and elegant organic forms, such as asymmetrical vases, bulbous bottles, fazzoletto handkerchief bowls with wavy rims, and pale transparent bubbles. Colours are luminous amber, aquamarine, turquoise, lilac, milky white and rich red, with patchwork murrine mosaics, incalmo bands, delicate lattice threading and acid-etched matte surfaces. Smooth rounded shapes, light-catching, subtle imperfection, mid-century Italian jewel-like sculptural glass in a gallery vitrine.'),
('Barovier and Toso', 'Europe', '1930s-60s', 'lighting', 'In the style of Barovier and Toso, Murano glass chandeliers and lighting with arms of hand-blown transparent glass flowers, leaves and curling ribbons, in clear crystal, rose pink, aqua and amber. Large elaborate Rezzonico-style chandeliers with ornate scrolling branches and floral cups, and mid-century sculptural versions with cascading glass tubes or rods and ball pendants in white and gold. Glossy, translucent, ornate, festive Venetian palace ballroom glitter, delicate curved arms around a central metal column.'),
('Lalique', 'Europe', '1920s', 'glass', 'In the style of Lalique, French Art Deco moulded glass in frosted opalescent and crystal clear, with relief decoration of flowers, birds, dragonflies, nude female figures, fish and leaping gazelles. Satin matte frosting contrasted with polished highlights, pale ice-blue and amber tinted glass, black enamel details and geometric stylised borders. Vases, perfume bottles, car mascots and chandeliers with a glowing crystal sparkle, sinuous curves, elegant and refined Parisian luxury.'),
('Daum', 'Europe', '1900s', 'glass', 'In the style of Daum, French Art Nouveau cameo and pate de verre glass, thick layered vessels with acid-etched and wheel-carved decoration of thistles, poppies, irises, mountain landscapes and winter scenes. Mottled colours graded from smoky orange to deep green, milky mist, powder blue and amber, with enamelled and gilded highlights. Soft translucent bodies, naturalistic plant forms swelling around bulbous vases and lamp shades, rich and dreamy, subdued glow like looking through frosted weather.'),
('Baccarat', 'Europe', '19th century', 'glass', 'In the style of Baccarat, French lead crystal tableware and lighting, clear and brilliant with deep geometric diamond cuts, fluted columns, faceted stoppers and heavy bases. Stemware with cut hobnail diamonds and sparkling prismatic edges, ornate chandeliers with tiers of pendant drops and gilded bronze arms, decanters, vases and bright red cut-glass candlesticks. Dazzling refraction, rainbow highlights, luxury dining table set under candlelight, formal and opulent Second Empire palace feel.'),
('Orrefors', 'Europe', '1930s-50s', 'glass', 'In the style of Orrefors, Swedish art glass, thick crystal-clear vessels with deep engraved or wheel-cut scenes, ethereal Graal pieces with trapped air bubbles and abstract wavy colour patterns, and Ariel glass with internal air traps. Streamlined heavy bowls and tapering vases, smooth heavy walls, cool transparent palette with accents of slate blue, smoky grey and soft green. Understated, refined, sculptural Scandinavian modernism, pure and sparkling in cold light.'),
('Kosta Boda', 'Europe', '1980s-90s', 'glass', 'In the style of Kosta Boda, Swedish contemporary art glass, bold and colourful hand-blown pieces with chunky abstract forms, bright stripes, spotted and swirled colour layers, and tall vases with cheerful faces, birds, fish, cat shapes and pastel clowns. Thick transparent bodies, saturated magenta, cobalt, orange, emerald and cool teal swirls, glossy smooth surfaces and organic asymmetrical silhouettes. Joyful, playful, sculptural, gallery shelf display with light refracting through thick glass.'),
('Iittala', 'Europe', '1950s', 'glass', 'In the style of Iittala, Finnish glass and tableware with organic fluid forms, such as undulating leaf-shaped bowls, free-form vases with wavy rims like lake shores, simple cylindrical tumblers with a ring of bumps, and bird sculptures in coloured glass. Palette of crystal clear, smoky grey, sea green, cobalt blue, burnt orange and ruby. Smooth, rounded, minimal and soft, with moulded ripples evoking ice, water and birch bark, Nordic calm and functional beauty.'),
('Arabia', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Arabia, Finnish stoneware and porcelain with simple rounded cylindrical and bowl shapes, stackable cups, plates and teapots with sturdy loop handles. Glazes in cream white, matte brown, ochre, forest green, mustard and speckled grey, or bright flat 1970s orange, yellow and brown abstract flowers and mushrooms in bold stencil and stripe patterns. Chunky, warm, earthy, practical, plain with hand-painted irregularity, cosy Nordic kitchen.'),
('Royal Copenhagen', 'Europe', '18th century-present', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Royal Copenhagen, Danish porcelain with hand-painted cobalt blue underglaze patterns on white, such as ribbed fluted edges with delicate lace-like pierced rims, small blue flowers and intricate half-lace and full-lace motifs. Tableware, tureens and ornamental figurines with soft pastel overglaze, three small wavy lines as base mark, thin translucent body, crisp brushwork, symmetrical and orderly, heirloom dining table elegance.'),
('Bing and Grondahl', 'Europe', '1890s-1950s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Bing and Grondahl, Danish porcelain in soft blue-grey and white, famous for underglaze tableware with elegant seagull and heron motifs, stylised flowers and tall reeds in shaded cobalt, plus delicate relief-moulded Christmas plates with winter village scenes. Thin glazed white porcelain, naturalistic Art Nouveau brushwork in muted pastel greys, creams, sea blues and lilac, smooth curved teapots, vases and figurines with crackled and sculpted surfaces, delicate and serene.'),
('Wedgwood', 'Europe', '18th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Wedgwood, English jasperware with matte unglazed stoneware in pale powder blue, sage green, lilac, black and cream, decorated with crisp white relief figures in classical Greek and Roman scenes, garlands, urns, putti and acanthus borders. Vases, cameo plaques, teapots and trinket boxes with fine sharp sprigged moulding applied to a smooth chalky background, along with creamy glazed tableware. Neoclassical symmetry, elegant and delicate, drawing-room mantel decoration.'),
('Spode', 'Europe', '19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Spode, English transferware pottery with dense blue-and-white underglaze printing of an Italian landscape with a classical ruin, a bridge, a tower and trees, framed by a border of flowers and shell-like motifs. Cream-white earthenware plates, platters, tureens, teapots and jugs with intricately engraved line shading in deep indigo blue, also Chinese-style willow landscapes, floral chintz and red or green transfer variants. Cottage dresser display, charming and traditional with an old-world look.'),
('Royal Doulton', 'Europe', '1900s-1930s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Royal Doulton, English ceramics ranging from stoneware vases with Art Nouveau tube-lined flowers in earthy brown, blue and green, to mottled red-and-black flambe glaze with running streaks, and hand-painted bone china figurines of ladies in crinoline gowns and character jugs with grinning caricature faces. Glossy, richly coloured, finely detailed with pastel flesh tones, floral garlands, gilded rims, and sculpted ruffles. Sentimental Victorian and Edwardian parlour cabinet display.'),
('Newport Pottery', 'Europe', '1930s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Newport Pottery Bizarre ware, English Art Deco earthenware hand-painted with bold geometric zigzags, triangles, diamonds, stylised trees, houses and flowers in bright enamel orange, yellow, red, green, blue and purple, with black outlines on creamy glaze. Angular conical teapots with triangular handles, stepped sugar shakers, cubist cups, bulbous jugs, sunrise and crocus patterns. Cheerful, vivid, jazzy, gloriously flat and modernist 1930s tea table.'),
('Meissen', 'Europe', '18th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Meissen, German hard-paste porcelain, lustrous white with exquisitely hand-painted scattered flowers, vividly coloured birds and chinoiserie scenes. Rococo tableware, gilded scrolling borders, applied sculpted flowers and delicate lace-draped porcelain figures of shepherdesses, courtiers and harlequins with pink cheeks, dainty gestures and pastel costumes. Blue crossed swords mark in underglaze, onion pattern in cobalt blue and iron red, luxurious, fragile, baroque palace cabinet showpiece.'),
('Sevres', 'Europe', '18th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Sevres, French soft-paste and hard-paste porcelain with intensely coloured ground glazes in deep royal blue, turquoise, apple green and rose pink, framed by gold gilding and reserved panels painted with birds, flowers, pastoral lovers and cherubs. Rococo vase and tureen shapes with scrolled handles and ormolu mounts, white biscuit porcelain figures. Opulent, ornate, gleaming gold, refined courtly Versailles taste.'),
('Royal Worcester', 'Europe', '19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Royal Worcester, English porcelain with hand-painted naturalistic subjects such as fruit, fallen blossoms, game birds, highland cattle and landscapes on ivory ground, framed by raised gilding, jewelled enamel dots and pierced reticulated edges. Rich cream and blush ivory glaze, gold scrolling, oriental-inspired shapes, shell-shaped dishes, ornamental ewers and dessert services, finely detailed Victorian elegance, and pot-pourri vases with delicate floral sprays and handles of twisting branches.'),
('Haviland Limoges', 'Europe', '19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Limoges porcelain houses, French white hard-paste dinnerware with delicate hand-painted pastel roses, violets and wildflower sprays, pale pink, mint and lavender scalloped edges with gold rims, moulded basketweave and lace patterns. Thin translucent bright white body, soft floral garlands, perfectly rounded teacups with curled handles, dessert plates, fine trinket boxes and lidded tureens. Light, romantic, feminine, cottage garden and Belle Epoque tea service charm.'),
('De Porceleyne Fles', 'Europe', '17th century-present', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Delft Royal Blue, Dutch tin-glazed earthenware painted by hand in rich cobalt blue on glossy white, depicting windmills, canals, sailing ships, tulips, milkmaids, farmhouses and floral scrolls, with fine brushwork and blue shading. Tiles, plates, tulip vases, clogs, and tall pyramid-shaped flower vases with multiple spouts. Slightly crackled glaze, soft blue-white contrast, charming, folksy Dutch heritage with elegant Chinese-inspired scenes.'),
('Faberge', 'Russia and Eastern Europe', '1890s-1910s', 'decorative arts', 'In the style of Faberge, Imperial Russian jewelled objects, especially egg-shaped caskets in layered translucent guilloche enamel in pastel pink, powder blue, mint green, lilac and cream, over engraved sunburst patterns, framed by gold, pearls, diamonds and rubies. Miniature surprise inside, tiny gold chariots and portraits, hardstone animals carved in jade, agate and rock crystal, silver cigarette cases and picture frames, delicate gilded neoclassical garlands, bows and laurel wreaths. Opulent, precious, exact, royal treasury glitter.'),
('Tiffany and Co', 'North America', '19th-20th century', 'silverware', 'In the style of Tiffany and Co, American fine silverware, jewellery and gift objects presented in a signature robin-egg pale turquoise blue with white satin ribbon. Sterling silver flatware with bold chased patterns, engraved leaf and shell borders, repousse flowers, hammered Japanese-influenced surfaces with mixed metals, tall silver tea services and trophy cups, solitaire diamond rings in six-prong platinum settings. Clean, polished and prestigious, minimal sans-serif engraved lettering, bright white gleam.'),
('Tiffany Studios', 'North America', '1900s', 'lighting', 'In the style of Tiffany Studios, American Art Nouveau stained-glass table lamps with domed shades built from hundreds of small leaded opalescent glass pieces in rich greens, ambers, deep blues, orange and red, shaped into dragonflies, wisteria, peonies, poppies, dogwood and geometric borders. Bronze bases cast as tree trunks, lily pads or twisting stems with dark green-brown patina, favrile iridescent glass vases in peacock blue and gold, glowing jewel-like light, lush naturalistic mood.'),
('Georg Jensen', 'Europe', '1900s-1950s', 'silverware', 'In the style of Georg Jensen, Danish sterling silver in softly hammered, organic sculptural forms, with smooth rounded bulbous bodies, grape clusters, berries, blossoms and curling leaves, and later streamlined modernist plain silver with sensuous curves. Flatware with fluid, bulging handles, teapots with carved ebony or ivory-coloured knobs and handles, bowls with openwork stems, brooches and pendants with cabochon stones. Gleaming matte silver, restrained, elegant and handcrafted Scandinavian luxury.'),
('Christofle', 'Europe', '1920s-30s', 'silverware', 'In the style of Christofle, French silver-plated tableware with strong Art Deco geometry, smooth cylindrical and faceted shapes, classic beaded and ribbed edges, and engraved monogram cartouches. Cocktail shakers, ice buckets, serving trays and candelabra in mirror-polished silver with ebony or wooden handles, thick fluted flatware, banded rims and pared down lines. Crisp elegant reflections, luxurious dinner table with white linen and crystal, grand ocean liner dining salon.'),
('Stickley', 'North America', '1900s-10s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Stickley, American Arts and Crafts Mission furniture in solid quarter-sawn oak with visible straight grain and ray flecks, rectilinear boxy forms, vertical slats, flat panels, exposed mortise-and-tenon joinery with pegs and keys, and wide plank arms. Dark fumed brown finish, hammered copper or iron hardware, thick leather or canvas cushions on drop-in seats, bookcases with leaded glass doors, rocking chairs and settles. Honest, sturdy, handmade, simple lodge-like craftsman living room.'),
('Gillows', 'Europe', '18th-19th century', 'furniture', 'In the style of Gillows, English Georgian and Regency furniture made from rich figured mahogany, rosewood and satinwood with crisp neoclassical lines, reeded tapering legs, brass inlay, ebony stringing, and ornate lion-paw feet. Davenports, pedestal sideboards, library tables with leather inlay tops, sabre-leg chairs, secretaire bookcases and brass castors. Deep polished red-brown wood glow, formal symmetry, refined country house and gentlemen club interior.'),
('Liberty', 'Europe', '1890s-1900s', 'textiles', 'In the style of Liberty, English Aesthetic Movement and Arts and Crafts textiles and furnishings, with fine cotton lawn and silk printed in small-scale floral patterns, paisley, peacock feathers, stylised tulips and Celtic knotwork in soft jewel colours of plum, teal, rose, olive, mustard and indigo. Furniture in oak with simple pewter and copper fittings with beaten decoration, and Tudor-revival timber-framed shopfront mood. Delicate, artistic, bohemian, romantic Victorian drawing room.'),
('Morris and Co', 'Europe', '1860s-1900s', 'textiles', 'In the style of Morris and Co, English Arts and Crafts wallpaper and textiles with dense, flat, intertwined foliage, acanthus leaves, pomegranates, willow boughs, honeysuckle, tulips and birds, repeating in rhythmic symmetrical trellises and curving vines. Muted natural dyes of indigo blue, madder red, moss green, russet, olive and ochre on cream. Woodblock-printed, tapestry and embroidery look, hand-drawn with a medieval flavour, restful and rich, cottage and manor room hangings.'),
('Wiener Werkstatte', 'Europe', '1900s-1920s', 'decorative arts', 'In the style of Wiener Werkstatte, Viennese Secession craftsmanship with geometric abstraction, strict grids of black and white squares, concentric circles, stylised roses, wavy lines and hand-block-printed bold patterns in orange, coral, turquoise, black and gold. Silver and metalwork with pierced squares, ebonised wood, enamelled jewellery, elongated chairs with grid-patterned backs, ceramics with chequered bands and stylised flowers. Sophisticated, rhythmic, ornamental modernism with a precise linear elegance.'),
('Bauhaus workshops', 'Europe', '1920s', 'furniture', 'In the style of the Bauhaus workshops, German functional modernism using primary geometry, circles, squares and triangles, with tubular steel chairs, chromed frames, black leather straps, flat plywood, bent wood and white-painted walls. Palette of primary red, yellow and blue with black, white and grey. Slim cantilever stools, nesting tables, geometric tea infusers in nickel, tapestries with abstract rectangles and woven grids, lamps of opal glass spheres on nickel stems, sans-serif lowercase lettering. Rational, austere, factory-ready elegance.'),
('Shaker workshops', 'North America', '19th century', 'furniture', 'In the style of Shaker workshops, American utilitarian furniture and oval boxes in pine, maple and cherry with plain, tapered, turned legs, simple ladder-back chairs with woven tape seats, peg rails on walls, delicate swallowtail-joined oval bentwood boxes, and plain painted finishes in barn red, mustard yellow, blue-green and milk-paint grey. Clean lines, no ornament, honest dovetails, spare, serene, tidy village room with sunlight, light handmade perfection.'),
('Heals', 'Europe', '1900s-1930s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Heals, English Arts and Crafts and early modern furniture in plain, light limed oak and fumed oak, with simple rectilinear cabinets, square-section legs, chamfered edges, brass or iron handles, cut-out hearts, and tall wardrobes with slender proportions. Painted pastel beds and chests with delicate stencilled flowers, bold geometric printed linen and cotton fabrics in modern greens, oranges and inky blues. Tidy, sensible, cottage-modern bedroom and living room look.'),
('Habitat', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'homeware', 'In the style of Habitat, British swinging-sixties high street homeware, simple and affordable, with cheerful bright striped and checked cotton, white and primary-coloured enamel pots, chunky pine furniture, stackable wooden tables, earthenware crocks and mugs, white porcelain, wire baskets, paper lanterns, rush matting and bright rugs. Colours are red, yellow, white, orange and natural pine. Casual, youthful, continental bistro-style kitchen, plants, bare floors, plain white walls, sociable and unfussy.'),
('Ercol', 'Europe', '1950s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Ercol, English post-war furniture in pale elm and beech, with slender spindle backs, sweeping hoops and curved arms, splayed tapering legs, and simple bentwood construction. Light blond finishes and darker stained elm with visible swirling grain, round-cornered sideboards with sliding doors and tapered feet, daybeds and stacking chairs with spoke-like backs. Cushions in rust, olive and mustard tweed. Warm, domestic, gentle, suburban 1950s sitting room.'),
('G-Plan', 'Europe', '1950s-60s', 'furniture', 'In the style of G-Plan, British mid-century teak and afrormosia furniture, low sleek sideboards with sliding doors, tapered round legs, and angular brass cup handles, plus fresco-style two-tone cabinets with white and black laminate panels. Sculptural sofas with slim wooden arms and chunky tweed cushions in orange, mustard, olive and chocolate, round-ended coffee tables, wall units, and teak room dividers. Rich orange-brown oiled grain, optimistic, comfortable, suburban 1960s living room.'),
('Parker Knoll', 'Europe', '1930s-60s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Parker Knoll, British reclining wing-back armchairs with deep padded seat cushions, tall sloping high backs with ears, and shaped, polished walnut or mahogany arms with turned fronts, resting on short curving legs. Upholstery in floral chintz, tapestry weave, brocade, mustard velvet or green moquette, buttoned details and fringed or piped seams. Cosy, grandmotherly, comfortable, rocker-recliner mechanism hidden under a skirted base, traditional lounge by a gas fire.'),
('Hille', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Hille, British modernist moulded polypropylene furniture, with one-piece stacking chairs on four splayed legs, smooth seamless shells in primary red, orange, white, black and lime, rounded rectangular seats and gently flared backs. Plastic cubes, plywood tables and plain bent-ply screens, shiny high-impact polymer surfaces with matte texture, simple geometry and mass-produced elegance. Pop, optimistic, space-age 1960s school, canteen and office look.'),
('Sanderson', 'Europe', '1860s-1960s', 'textiles', 'In the style of Sanderson, English wallpaper and chintz fabrics with large-scale painterly blooms, cabbage roses, peonies, hydrangeas, hand-drawn trailing leaves, birds and berries, and printed willow patterns. Colour palette of soft pink, duck-egg blue, sage green, cream, mulberry and gold, in printed cotton, linen union and embossed wall coverings, plus mid-century abstract botanical prints. Graceful, romantic, traditional English country house room with curtains, cushions and armchairs.'),
('Cole and Son', 'Europe', '19th century-present', 'wallpaper', 'In the style of Cole and Son, English hand-block-printed wallpaper, dense and lavish, with chinoiserie pagodas and flowering branches, hand-drawn exotic birds, oversized banana leaves, monkeys, lush tropical foliage and woodland animals. Rich colours of petrol blue, emerald, burnt orange, coral and charcoal against metallic gold or silver grounds, flocked velvety textures, damask motifs and stripes. Theatrical, elegant, bold hallway and dining room walls from floor to ceiling, collectible and luxurious.'),
('Le Creuset', 'Europe', '1950s-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Le Creuset, French enamelled cast-iron cookware, heavy round and oval casserole pots with domed lids and fat loop handles, finished in high-gloss glazes of flame orange, deep red, Mediterranean blue, sunny yellow, forest green and cream, with matte black interior. Gradient volcanic orange, thick rolled rim, a bulbous knob, rounded, sturdy and generous. Kettles, skillets and ramekins in matching shiny colours, warm, rustic, farmhouse kitchen glamour.'),
('Staub', 'Europe', '1970s-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Staub, French cast-iron cookware with matte black enamel interior and darkly glossy, speckled exterior in grenadine red, deep blue, graphite and basil green, heavy round and oval cocottes with self-basting spiked lids, and lids topped by a brass or nickel animal-shaped knob like a cockerel, cat or pumpkin. Chunky vegetable-shaped baking dishes, tomato and cabbage shaped pots. Rustic, weighty, restaurant-grade, traditional French bistro cooking.'),
('Denby', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Denby, English stoneware tableware in rich, earthy, drippy glazes, with chunky rounded casseroles, mugs, plates and jugs, wax-resist patterns and tactile dark rims. Colours are deep brown, mustard, blue-green, olive, smoky grey-blue and cream, speckled and reactive with natural variation, in brown-and-cream swirled and pebble-textured designs. Heavy, hand-thrown look, warm, practical, rustic oven-to-table and retro 1970s dining room.'),
('Pyrex', 'North America', '1950s-70s', 'homeware', 'In the style of Pyrex, American glass bakeware and opal milk glass mixing bowls, nesting in sets of four with rounded shapes, in sunny primary colours of red, yellow, green and blue, or printed with mid-century patterns such as butterprint barns, friendship daisies, gooseberry, snowflake and starburst in turquoise, pink, avocado green, mustard and white. Casseroles with clear lids, loaf pans with rolled handles. Cheerful, bright, nostalgic farmhouse kitchen and diner.'),
('Fiestaware', 'North America', '1930s-50s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Fiestaware, American Art Deco dinnerware in thick, glossy, solid-colour glazes of cobalt blue, vivid red-orange, yellow, light green, ivory and turquoise, with concentric ring-shaped ridges around plates and bowls, round handles, banded rims, bulbous pitchers and sharp-edged ring-handled cups. Colourful mix-and-match settings on a plain table. Cheerful, durable, bold diner and kitchen look with rounded, streamlined shapes.'),
('Tupperware', 'North America', '1950s-70s', 'homeware', 'In the style of Tupperware, American mid-century plastic storage containers, translucent, slightly frosted polyethylene with soft rounded corners, airtight lids with a raised central burp seal, nesting bowls, canisters, pitchers and jello moulds. Colours include avocado green, harvest gold, tangerine, pale turquoise, pink, mustard and almond. Matte waxy finish, stacked in neat towers, retro suburban kitchen, optimistic housewife-party look and joyful household order.'),
('Lodge', 'North America', '19th century-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Lodge, American cast-iron cookware, heavy black skillets with a pour spout on each side, a long handle ending in a hanging hole, rough pebbly matte seasoned surface, deep Dutch ovens with bail handles, griddles with ridged bottoms, and cornbread pans shaped like corn cobs. Matte charcoal black with slightly rusty edges and glossy brown seasoning, plain, indestructible, campfire and cabin kitchen, rustic and honest.'),
('Nambu ironworks', 'East Asia', '17th century-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Nambu ironworks, Japanese cast-iron tetsubin kettles and teapots, rounded bulging bodies with arare pattern, rows of small raised bumps like hailstones, topped with a small knob lid, a swing handle of iron or bronze, and a short curved spout. Matte black, deep brown or rust-coloured finish, sometimes with inlaid silver or relief motifs of pine, cranes, plum blossoms and waves. Heavy, weighty, tea ceremony quietness, simple, wabi-sabi and austere.'),
('Arita porcelain', 'East Asia', '17th-19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Arita porcelain, Japanese white porcelain with crisp underglaze cobalt blue paintings of landscapes, pines, bamboo, cranes and flowers, and enamelled colourful versions in red, green, yellow and sky blue on milky white body with generous empty space. Thin elegant dishes, octagonal bowls, bottle vases, lidded jars with minimalist asymmetrical compositions, delicate brushstrokes, clear sparkling glaze. Refined, airy, graceful, tea house tableware.'),
('Imari ware', 'East Asia', '17th-19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Imari ware, Japanese porcelain richly decorated with a dense palette of underglaze cobalt blue, iron-red overglaze and gold, with panelled chrysanthemums, peonies, phoenixes, brocade patterns, fans and waves on large plates, bowls, jars and lidded urns. Sections of deep blue alternate with fiery red and gilded floral scrolls, leaving little blank white, flamboyant, ornate, sumptuous like silk brocade, with scalloped rims and lobed bodies.'),
('Satsuma ware', 'East Asia', '19th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Satsuma ware, Japanese earthenware with a cream, finely crackled ivory glaze, covered in miniature, densely painted scenes of samurai, geisha, temple gardens, Mount Fuji and cherry blossoms in vivid enamels of red, green, blue, and lavish raised gold. Elaborate vases with lion-dog handles, koros with pierced lids, tea sets, lavish gold borders with brocade pattern bands. Highly detailed, glowing, export-style Meiji era jewel-like cabinet piece.'),
('Moser', 'Europe', '1900s-30s', 'glass', 'In the style of Moser, Bohemian crystal glassware with heavy cut and engraved decoration, gold-gilded rims, deeply cut facets, and etched floral and animal motifs such as stags, swans and acanthus. Intense transparent coloured glass in alexandrite purple, emerald green, cobalt, ruby, amber and rich smoky topaz, with enamelled gold frames and fluted columns. Rich, jewelled, Art Deco and Belle Epoque luxury, elegant stemware, decanters and vases glowing in warm lamp light.'),
('Tolix', 'Europe', '1930s', 'furniture', 'In the style of Tolix, French industrial pressed sheet-steel furniture, with a stackable A-shaped chair made of a single formed sheet of steel, rounded backrest with a perforated or plain seat, simple tapered tubular legs with reinforced foot caps. Matte lacquered, powder-coated and galvanised metal in red, dark green, yellow, black, grey and raw zinc, with slightly dented, utilitarian patina. Simple, cafe terrace and factory canteen look, tough, thin and urban.'),
('Marimekko', 'Europe', '1960s', 'textiles', 'In the style of Marimekko, Finnish bold graphic textiles and homeware in cotton printed with oversized abstract poppies, stripes, dots, geometric blocks and wobbly lines in saturated red, pink, orange, deep blue, black and white. Large-scale simplified flower shapes with hand-cut, screenprinted edges and flat colour fields, used on curtains, bed linen, tablecloths, tote bags, cups and trays. Cheerful, cool, graphic, liberated, Scandinavian modern kitchen and sunny window.'),
('Louis Poulsen', 'Europe', '1920s-60s', 'lighting', 'In the style of Louis Poulsen, Danish pendant lamps with layered concentric shades that conceal the bulb, curved overlapping discs in white, copper, brass and chrome, forming a glare-free soft glow, and artichoke-shaped lamps made of dozens of overlapping leaves in polished steel or white. Smooth, sculptural, symmetrical, with warm reflections on a dining table. Elegant, calm, restrained Scandinavian hanging light.'),
('Anglepoise', 'Europe', '1930s', 'lighting', 'In the style of Anglepoise, British spring-balanced task lamp, with two long slender arms and exposed coiled springs, jointed pivots, a conical metal shade, and a heavy stepped round base with a switch. Enamel or powder-coated metal in cream, black, red, grey, racing green and polished chrome. Industrial, technical, balanced and flexible, posed in mid-air like a drawing compass, studio desk, drawing office and workshop atmosphere.'),
('Moorcroft', 'Europe', '1900s-30s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Moorcroft, English art pottery with tube-lined, hand-painted designs of pomegranates, orchids, wisteria, toadstools and Art Nouveau flowers, outlined in raised slip lines like cloisonne. Deep, jewel-toned glazes of royal blue, forest green, burgundy, plum and gold, with rich flambe runs and glossy, smooth finishes. Rounded vases, bowls and ginger jars, luminous and velvety, collectible Edwardian shelf piece.'),
('Emma Bridgewater', 'Europe', '1990s-present', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Emma Bridgewater, British earthenware in cream-glazed, spongeware style with hand-sponged blue, red and green spots, dotty hearts, stars, polka dots, and cheerful stripes, along with bold black lettering mottoes and rustic farm animals like hens, pigs and sheep. Chunky mugs, jugs, teapots and plates with painterly, irregular edges and speckled glaze. Cheerful, cottagey, homely kitchen dresser and Sunday breakfast table.'),
('Portmeirion', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Portmeirion, British tableware of embossed botanical designs, with illustrated flowers, ferns, fruit, butterflies and bees in naturalistic colour on cream or white ground, dense with leaves and vines and wide-rimmed plates with scalloped edges. Chunky mugs, tall jugs, cake stands, with bold rich colours of burgundy, fern green, gold and cobalt blue. Cottage garden, apothecary, Victorian botanical print-book mood, cosy and abundant.'),
('Rosenthal', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Rosenthal, German modern porcelain with smooth, sleek, pure white forms, rounded cylinder cups, geometric ribs, clean silhouettes, thin gold or platinum rims, and abstract hand-painted or transfer patterns in black, cobalt, orange and brown. Plain studio-line vases with relief carving, bold stripes, pastel bands, and 1970s psychedelic patterns. Crisp, glossy, translucent, elegant yet casual, modernist dinner service and gallery shelf.'),
('Lomonosov Porcelain', 'Russia and Eastern Europe', '1920s', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Lomonosov Porcelain, Russian Imperial porcelain, including its revolutionary 1920s Suprematist and agitprop work, white thin cups, plates and teapots with geometric abstract red, black and white shapes, hammer and sickle motifs, stars, factories, bold angular lettering, and stylised propaganda figures. Also the classic cobalt net pattern with gilded cell edges and white relief bumps. Striking graphic energy, flat bold colours, historical museum display.'),
('Gzhel', 'Russia and Eastern Europe', '17th century-present', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Gzhel, Russian folk ceramics painted in cobalt blue on bright white glaze, with brushstrokes in varied blue tones, flowing flowers, leaves, scrolls, dots and drops, on teapots, tea sets, samovar-shaped vessels, plates and glossy figurines of animals, birds and women in traditional dress. Fluid, smooth strokes shading from deep ink to pale sky blue, joyful and fresh, with a wonderful clean blue-white contrast and handmade charm.'),
('Khokhloma', 'Russia and Eastern Europe', '17th century-present', 'woodwork', 'In the style of Khokhloma, Russian folk painted woodenware, turned bowls, spoons, ladles, cups and trays painted with glowing gold-like swirling patterns on black or deep red lacquer, creating curling vines, rowan berries, strawberries, leaves and flowers in red, black, gold and green. Glossy varnish hardened by oven firing, shiny golden-yellow undertone, rich, warm, curvilinear, festive, fairy-tale peasant kitchen treasure.'),
('Kutahya and Iznik ceramics', 'Middle East', '16th-18th century', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Kutahya and Iznik ceramics, Ottoman fritware tiles, plates and mosque lamps painted under a clear glaze with intense cobalt blue, turquoise, sage green, tomato red and white, in patterns of tulips, carnations, hyacinths, rosebuds, saz leaves, and curling arabesques. Radiating floral rosettes, repeated flowers on tile panels, symmetrical and flowing. Glossy, bright, crisp, elegant, a mosque wall and bazaar shelf look.'),
('Talavera de Puebla', 'Latin America', '17th century-present', 'ceramics', 'In the style of Talavera de Puebla, Mexican tin-glazed earthenware with a thick, creamy white glossy glaze painted by hand with cobalt blue, yellow, green, orange and black motifs of flowers, birds, vines, geometric borders and Moorish-inspired arabesques. Plates, tiles, vases, jugs and sinks with slightly uneven edges and drips, bold brushwork, rustic, festive, sunlit courtyard and hacienda kitchen, joyful colour.'),
('Royal Selangor', 'Southeast Asia', '1900s-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Royal Selangor, Malaysian pewter tableware, polished silvery grey, soft lustrous metal with hammered or smooth finish, in tankards, bowls, tea sets, trays and vases, adorned with engraved or embossed motifs of hibiscus flowers, bamboo, batik-like flowers and rope borders. Heavy-bottomed, rounded forms with simple handles, sometimes mixed with dark wood or leather accents. Soft, bright, cool gleam, refined, tropical colonial table.'),
('Dinosaur Designs', 'Oceania', '1990s-present', 'homeware', 'In the style of Dinosaur Designs, Australian handmade resin homeware and jewellery, swirling, marbled, translucent coloured resin in bright pink, coral, sea green, cobalt, sunny yellow and smoky amber, poured and cast into chunky organic pebble, wave and shell shapes. Bowls, servers, vases, candlesticks and salad hands with smooth glossy surfaces, marbled colour streaks with air-like depth and fluid imperfect edges. Sensuous, beachy, playful, sculptural, bright summer table.'),
]
